WEBVTT

NOTE Birch & Co, Nordic entry kick-off. Friday 4 September 2026. Speakers: Theo Marsh, Iris Bell, Sam Rivera.

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.500
<v Theo Marsh>Sam, welcome aboard. Iris runs this day to day. I'll come in for the decisions.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:17.000
<v Sam Rivera>Thanks, Theo. As I understand it, you want to know whether the Nordics are worth entering next year, and if they are, how.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:27.000
<v Theo Marsh>That's it. And if the numbers don't hold up, I'd rather hear it in September than in March.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:38.000
<v Iris Bell>The board meets on the twenty-eighth. Whatever we take to them has to be a recommendation, not a menu.

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:52.000
<v Sam Rivera>Then I'd work in three pieces. Market sizing first, with a memo by the sixteenth. Then which carrier gets you there. Then a launch plan, once the board has said yes.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:01:01.000
<v Iris Bell>I can send you our distributor contacts in the region. We met six of them at the trade fair in June.

00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:05.000
<v Sam Rivera>That would help. By Monday?

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.000
<v Iris Bell>Monday the seventh, yes.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:21.000
<v Theo Marsh>One more thing. I know you work across the industry. I don't want to know who else you work for, and I don't want them knowing about us.

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:28.000
<v Sam Rivera>That's how I work anyway. Nothing from one client goes into another client's work. You have my word on it.

00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:31.000
<v Theo Marsh>Good. Then let's get going.
